This complete program compares two temperatures using the same ideas as scores.

```swift
func compareTemperatures(_ first: Int, _ second: Int) -> String {
    if first > second {
        return "warmer"
    }
    if first < second {
        return "cooler"
    }
    return "equal"
}
print(compareTemperatures(16, 11))
print(compareTemperatures(6, 11))
print(compareTemperatures(11, 11))
```

The printed results are warmer, cooler, and equal. func starts a function definition. The function's name is followed by its inputs in parentheses. -> String says that each call gives back text. return ends that call and sends a value back.

